Check of the moralization dataset, October 23, 2026

Potential problems found in the data
The diet screening isn’t working. Three self-described vegetarians were assigned to a group and completed the study. The prereg says vegetarians, vegans and pescatarians are screened out. Also, the diet answer options aren’t in the questionnaire (it only has a placeholder). In the data, “Neither Vegeterian nor Vegan” has a typo, and there’s no pescatarian option.
Forced response is missing on Q07. One respondent (R_8z1rY4gjEBjnRyV) skipped all 12 perceived-harm items, even though the questionnaire and prereg say every answer is required.
Q11 may be miscoded. All 6 respondents have “yogurt” and none have “yogurt plant”. Every other choice item varies, so please check whether the soya yogurt option was given the “yogurt plant” recode in Qualtrics.
“Finished” can’t identify completers. Screened-out vegans have Finished = True and Progress = 100. The prereg exclusion rule (“did not complete”) needs another indicator, such as Last Seen Flow Element ID (FL_29 for screen-outs, FL_16 for completers) or a group/end-of-survey flag.
The id column is empty for everyone.

These points need clarification:
What does VU treatment (values 0/1/2) mean? It’s filled only for the VU group and doesn’t match the Q03 treatment. I’m guessing it’s the second study’s condition, but please confirm.
The randomization orders aren’t exported. The prereg describes randomized block, item and left/right orders, but there are no display-order columns. If you want to check or control for presentation order, turn on “Export randomized viewing order” in Qualtrics.
The Q04 wording differs. Qualtrics shows “When thinking about the text, … emotions”; the questionnaire and prereg say “While reading the text…”.
The MFQ scoring keys are my assumption. I used Q22_1–3 and Q23_1–3 for care, Q22_4–6 and Q23_4–6 for purity, and Q22_7 (math) and Q23_7 (do good) as fillers. That gives 6 items per foundation, matching the prereg. Please confirm.
Some data quality points (likely test data). Five of the 9 rows are flagged Q_DuplicateRespondent, completion durations range from 123 s to 5,326 s, and two respondents gave the same answer to every MFQ item. One control respondent failed the attention check.
Some socio-demographic items need a look, even though they’re outside the scope of this check. Q38 asks for annual income but its question text says “each month”. Q39 food spending is free text with no currency. One birth year is 1926. Q29 has typos (“infomation”, “reluction”). Q45 labels contain trailing line breaks.

